ter/FlateDecode/ID[ ]/Info 407 0 R/Length 138/Root 409 0 R/Size 408/Type/XRef/W[1 3 1]>>stream h�bb\u0000\u0001&Fƒ� L �gA��)�}\u0017D �\u0001� � ��#X\\\u001bH2&\u0014��L���\u0013�x\u001d�� \"�/�H�m`\u0012,Μ\u0002\"\u0005�f2L\u0007�\u0004�����5�\b\u0003#v��\u000f\u0012�?>�(�~\u0011�r�\u001c%�'\u0019玆�(9��F��t5JR�d�\u0005�/\u0006�\u0000\u0003\u0000��\u001aF endstream endobj startxref 116 %%EOF","official":true,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-0-0","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":0,"timestampLabel":"0:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I'll call this meeting to order. Please stand for the Pledge of Allegiance. I pledge allegiance to the Flag of the United States of America and to the Republic for which it stands, one Nation, under God, indivisible, with liberty and justice for all. Thank you all very much. Please be seated. And I would like to open the second preliminary determination hearing.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1010-41","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1010,"timestampLabel":"16:50","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Motion carries. Now moving to our financial report. And for that, we bring back a friend from the past. Could you speak at the mic for cats? I'm sorry. It doesn't amplify in here, but it helps for the, yeah. Hello to everyone. And I'm glad to be back.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1038-42","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1038,"timestampLabel":"17:18","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- However, it's much better circumstances than it was six years ago. So I'm pleased with that. And I wish Matt well. I really do. This is his cash flow. And so primarily we look at the education fund and we look at the operations fund. And you know what the state's been doing a little bit with property tax movement. And so we're going to, for the next three years, pay real close attention to the operations fund.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1068-43","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1068,"timestampLabel":"17:48","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- It is going to be okay in 2026. They are allowing that 4 percent growth factor to enter in. But then in 2027 and 2028, they zeroed that out, and it is gone. So what they do with any kind of increase in the future there, it could be nothing, it could be 1, it could be 2 percent. So we will have to watch that. That is going to eat into the levy.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-108-4","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":108,"timestampLabel":"1:48","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- But I also know, just for purposes of the statute, that there's some statutorily required information here, some calculations that we had to run through, just like in the past when you guys have done control projects. And there's another stack. I brought out some extras, and Robin has them out in the lobby. So the project is, just for the record,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1095-44","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1095,"timestampLabel":"18:15","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And so we want to be really aware of that. When you get your cash flows, you want to pay attention to January 1st. You look at that number, January 1st, up in the upper left-hand corner, and you look at the last number over on the right-hand side in the little black box, December 31st, down there. And if those two numbers match up pretty close, your year is rolling along pretty good.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1123-45","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1123,"timestampLabel":"18:43","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And that's where you are. You're a little over 4 million, close to 5 million in January. You're 4 and 1 half million at the end of the year. And that's what you want to see. This is just kind of a snapshot of the future. The operations fund will be one, like I said, that will be interesting to watch. But it's doing the same thing right now. It's starting with a number, ending with a number that's very close to that, or maybe even a little bit higher. And that's OK.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1153-46","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1153,"timestampLabel":"19:13","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- You know, you always get into a debate about how much cash to keep in this fund, especially the education fund. When the state put the screws down on the operations fund and debt service fund and that and said you can only have 15% of it in cash like you used to carry 50% in debt service, now it's 15, your operations","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1180-47","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1180,"timestampLabel":"19:40","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- You've got to keep it lower because it moves your budget and affects the budget in a bad way when it comes to that fund when you do the budget in August, September. The education fund then carries more cash balance. It doesn't really have a number there that the state tracks or anything, but when you're spending $2 million a month on average, and if you look at your budget, it's around","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1208-48","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1208,"timestampLabel":"20:08","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- 20-some million, you're spending around two million every month. And so you've got to have a certain number there in hand, or if you don't and you fall too low there, you're going to be borrowing money to operate on. And you don't want to do that if you don't have to. Now, you know, there's ways to do it, but our goal is not to do that. So right now I'd say you're in pretty good shape.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1236-49","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1236,"timestampLabel":"20:36","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And like I said, we'll keep an eye on that operations fund as we move forward. Thank you. Thank you very much. Appreciate it. It'd be really good to have Paul back. It is, yes. And when I think back to when I became superintendent and the situation we were in back then, and it was really a great year working with Paul. And then when we brought Matt on board,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1266-50","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1266,"timestampLabel":"21:06","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- A lot of our financial success over the years can be traced back to Paul. We're glad to have him back working with us. We have him coming on Tuesdays so we can go to a China buffet restaurant for lunch. They don't do Mondays. That's something you don't want to forget. OK, well, welcome back.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1294-51","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1294,"timestampLabel":"21:34","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Now we'll turn to consideration to approve the preliminary determination in 1028 resolution. So Dr. Sanders. Actually we're gonna have Jacob come back up and talk to us about the purpose of the resolution. So again, so this outlines everything we discussed in those public hearings. It outlines the project that you've complied with the statute and we've combined, I know you'll recall a few years ago we would do these as separate","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1324-52","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1324,"timestampLabel":"22:04","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- resolutions, but we combined it into one since there's such overlap. And it makes the preliminary determination to proceed with the project, to proceed with the issuance of the bonds. It includes those parameters from Stiefel, the not to exceed $40 million, 20-year term max for each series of bonds, and the 7% max rate.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-133-5","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":133,"timestampLabel":"2:13","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- for various improvements, some renovations at the high school, which could include roof replacement, repair renovations and solar installation, band and choir expansion upgrades, improvements and renovations, constructing and equipping additional classrooms, constructing and equipping biomedical training classrooms,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1350-53","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1350,"timestampLabel":"22:30","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Stiefel will work with Jerry in sizing as you guys have needs and to make sure that the rate stays level given the impact with SB1.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1360-54","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1360,"timestampLabel":"22:40","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And again, assuming you guys adopt this, we'll put out a notice that starts at 30 day clock. We'll put out another notice at the same time, and we'll be back in September for another public hearing, and this time it'll be on the lease, and it'll cover kind of a lot of the same topics, but again, you want to have thoroughly considered everything and given the public a chance to comment. So with that, I'd be happy to answer any questions. Okay, any questions? This material we've been looking at for","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1390-55","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1390,"timestampLabel":"23:10","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Quite a while, huh? Okay. All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Thank you very much. We really appreciate all the work that you put in and helping","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1418-56","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1418,"timestampLabel":"23:38","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- keep us on track for this, I'd appreciate that. Okay, next is consideration to approve the course agreement, so Dr. Sanders. The annual agreement for the fire alarm sprinkler monitoring system is part of this agreement, it's a monthly service fee of $280.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1446-57","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1446,"timestampLabel":"24:06","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and also part of the agreement is a five-year plan for internal inspection of sprinkler pipes for the Edgewood Junior High School and Edgewood High School. The annual fee is $1,165 for the junior high and $2,093 for the high school. I recommend your approval. The course and agreement. Any discussion? All those in favor say aye.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1476-58","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1476,"timestampLabel":"24:36","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Opposed? Motion carries. Now consideration to approve the transportation handbook. So the transportation handbook was in desperate need of being updated. Audrey Myers, our director of transportation, has taken this summer to go through the handbook, update all of it, and I've listed for you in the board packet","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1500-59","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1500,"timestampLabel":"25:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- the different areas that the handbook covers, the general qualifications and conditions for employment, contract and fleet buses and drivers, information, general use and care of school buses, bus operation, transportation of students, routes, safety procedures and emergencies, and security and threat awareness. I recommend your approval.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-153-6","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":153,"timestampLabel":"2:33","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- installation and upgrades to turf at the baseball field, installation of turf and other improvements and upgrades at the softball field, technology office storage and workspace upgrades, replacements and equipping, parking and asphalt repair upgrades and replacements, tennis court repairs and renovations and other related renovations. At the high school, a list of renovations at the junior high, roof replacement, renovations and repair, solar installation,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1532-60","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1532,"timestampLabel":"25:32","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Second. Any discussion? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. No consideration to approve a memorandum of understanding with JAG Inc. All right. So unfortunately, we received really late in the summer that the Indiana Legislative Legislature approved the","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1562-61","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1562,"timestampLabel":"26:02","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- fiscal year 26, 27 by Annamen. Can't say that word. Yeah, state budget bill transitioning state funding for school dropout and prevention programming into a new freedom and opportunity in the education fund within the budget of the Department of Education. Essentially, this eliminated the state JAG funding from the Department of Workforce","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1591-62","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1591,"timestampLabel":"26:31","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- development's budget. However, the DOE chose not to provide funding for the JAG program. This has been a really effective program at the high school, really targets a very important population of students. So we worked with Sam Perkins, who's the manager of region eight, to use the grant's remaining dollars","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1620-63","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1620,"timestampLabel":"27:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- for 100% funding of the JAG position for the 2025-2026 school year. Under the new MOU, the JAG teacher will actually be an employee of RBBCSC, and we will submit reimbursements to the JAG grant to cover the cost of the JAG teacher. At this time,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1644-64","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1644,"timestampLabel":"27:24","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- We are committing to only one year continuation of the program. We're hoping that they will find funding somewhere to continue it after the 2025-26 school year. And we will be also evaluating the possibility of finding our own funds","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1669-65","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1669,"timestampLabel":"27:49","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- to continue the program and we'll try to have an answer back to the board in six to nine months in terms of whether or not we feel like we can continue JAG into the future. So I'm asking for the board to approve this MOU with the JAG organization. Approval. I second. Second, any discussion?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1696-66","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1696,"timestampLabel":"28:16","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Even though we're paying this person, we'll still use the JAG curriculum. They'll give us support, right? Yes, we're gonna continue to use the JAG curriculum. One more year? Yes. And then we're not doing it down in the junior high now, right? Right. Okay, so it's freshmen through seniors? We're hoping to have expanded to ninth through 12th grade at the high school this school year. Okay, all right, thanks. Any further discussion?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1726-67","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1726,"timestampLabel":"28:46","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Now we need to look at the JAG position itself. Senator? So basically, for all the things I've just said, we're asking since we have to have this position as an employee for RBB, we wanted to create the position of JAG instructor at Edgewood High School. I'll second.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1758-68","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1758,"timestampLabel":"29:18","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Any discussion? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Now we look to revisions of policies 4162 and 8510. Dr. Sanders? If you'll remember at the June school board meeting, I presented these two policy revisions as a first reading. Policy 4162 is drug and alcohol testing of CDL.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-178-7","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":178,"timestampLabel":"2:58","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- band choir expansion, upgrades, improvements and renovations, constructing and equipping additional classrooms, replacement of bleachers, parking and asphalt repair, upgrades and replacements, tennis court repairs and renovations and other related renovations.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1787-69","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1787,"timestampLabel":"29:47","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- holders and other employees who perform safety sensitive functions. It's really being revised at the direction of the Indiana State Police who do the inspections on our buses and suggested that our policy was not in line with their protocols. So we made those revisions.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1812-70","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1812,"timestampLabel":"30:12","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- We also made revisions to policy 8510, which is a wellness policy recommended by the Champs Committee, and it better aligns with the USDA smart snacks in school nutrition standards. Ferguson Law has reviewed both policies for compliance, and so I recommend your approval.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1842-71","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1842,"timestampLabel":"30:42","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Any discussion? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1851-72","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1851,"timestampLabel":"30:51","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Now we're going to look at the Administrator Assistance Agreements. Dr. Sanders? So it's interesting that we already have Paul come up and give a presentation. You haven't approved the contract yet. But you're familiar with this before when Paul came around the first time we used an organization called Administrative Assistance and they're a networked","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1876-73","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1876,"timestampLabel":"31:16","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- program throughout the whole state of Indiana that provides services to school corporations. It could be interim superintendent, interim principal, interim business manager, like we used Paul the first time. And this contract will be for $6,300 plus mileage and it'll go through July, 2026.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1902-74","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1902,"timestampLabel":"31:42","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And I listed for the board in the board packet all the things we'll be asking Paul to do. Mainly he's going to be doing the 2026 budget and at the same time training Debbie Tate in that process. And really Paul is going to follow the same formula that we used when we brought Matt in.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-191-8","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":191,"timestampLabel":"3:11","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and other renovations at the primary school and the intermediate school, including roof renovations and replacements and solar installation, playground expansion, asphalt patching, resurfacing, and parking improvements, and other related renovations. And I'll note just for the record, just for the public's purposes,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1931-75","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1931,"timestampLabel":"32:11","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And as you could tell, Paul did an amazing job training Matt. And so he's going to do the same thing with Debbie. And so I request that you approve this contract. The administrator assistance agreement. Second. Any discussion?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1955-76","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1955,"timestampLabel":"32:35","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I feel a lot more confident having Paul back to backstop us as we move forward here. Yes, yes. Kind of got near a ledge six years ago and he pulled us to safety, so he's our knight in shining armor. Any further discussion? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-1980-77","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":1980,"timestampLabel":"33:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- No, we turn to the Heritage Schools Agreement. And Jennifer Barrett, welcome to the front row here. It's after many years. I'm thankful that Paul also is here. I'm asking you to approve an agreement with Heritage Schools in Utah.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2003-78","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2003,"timestampLabel":"33:23","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- This is an agreement that we have with them to provide a free appropriate public education to one of our students who lives here within our district.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2014-79","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2014,"timestampLabel":"33:34","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Contract is effective from July 1st, 2025 to June 30th, 2026. Basically what this agreement says is that we will maintain the students individualized education plan, their IEP. We will monitor that through the school out in Utah. So we meet with them on a regular basis. They're a part of the students case conference committee. We receive general progress updates at least every nine weeks.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2044-80","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2044,"timestampLabel":"34:04","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- They allow us to be a part of that student's education in a setting that will meet his or her needs more effectively than what we can provide here for this particular student at Edgewood. I'm asking you to approve this agreement. Once it has been approved, we will go ahead and we will submit, along with Noah Dixon, our special education director,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2067-81","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2067,"timestampLabel":"34:27","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- who has just will be approved hopefully here shortly. Noah will start working on a seek application so that we can be reimbursed for the majority of these funds. Basically, the way that works is with the state of Indiana. Once a school board has approved the agreement, then we can start the application for seek.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2089-82","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2089,"timestampLabel":"34:49","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- There's no guarantee that we'll receive those excess costs. It's a finite number that the state puts into that fund, but the goal is that we give them everything they need in terms of that application so that we do receive that reimbursement on a monthly basis. And what's the value of the contract? The value of the contract overall. It's different for each kid. Let me pull that up for you, Dana.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2119-83","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2119,"timestampLabel":"35:19","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- This one is roughly $300,000. They do not break this down into individual hours, but they break it down into per hour, what they charge for.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2133-84","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2133,"timestampLabel":"35:33","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- the student services. So a lot of that will depend upon what the case conference committee decides. So when we meet again for this particular student coming up here in the next month and we'll be reworking that student's IEP, those hours could change depending upon the needs of that student at that time. So it depends on what type of services we're going to be adjusting from the previous IEP. So that is in this as far as the hourly amount or the daily amount that Heritage would charge for","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-215-9","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":215,"timestampLabel":"3:35","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- You're listing all the projects to authorize them. You won't necessarily do all those projects. It's just to authorize and to provide notice to the public of what you might do. As far as timing, this is the second preliminary hearing determination. Assuming you adopt the preliminary determination resolution, we would provide notice. There's a 30-day period when folks could remonstrate to have the referendum process apply.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2163-85","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2163,"timestampLabel":"36:03","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- those services. So for each one of these students, we're looking at roughly $250,000 to $300,000. Is that sufficient for Steven? Yes. Is that Exhibit A to the contract, the rates? Am I looking at the right thing? I am not sure on that, Christine. I don't think that one was for the full 365, Christine. It just showed for 200 days in the board packet.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2194-86","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2194,"timestampLabel":"36:34","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- show 200 days of special education and 365 days for room and board and therapeutic services. Correct. Yeah, we're paying for the full year, because they stay there year round. For Heritage, we're paying for 209 days of academic, 365 days for room and board, mental health, therapeutic services, just depending on what those look like for this individual student. So that is on number nine of the individual service agreement.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2224-87","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2224,"timestampLabel":"37:04","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And I think that's the same thing that's broken down on Exhibit A, which is page 243 of the packet. Yeah. OK. So I'm just going to make sure we cover everything. OK. I'll move approval of the Heritage Schools Incorporated Agreement. I'll second. Moved and seconded. Any discussion? Mr. Carano, is it time to move on to the next one, Ms. Barrett?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2253-88","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2253,"timestampLabel":"37:33","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- It is completely up to you. I asked her to kind of give us a quick overview of how this works. Because I know we just did this last year. And they're in our school district. We're going to give them the best care that they can get. For sure. But there were some things I was unaware of that we pay for. We also accommodate the families to help them travel to see their kids. That's part of the expense.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2277-89","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2277,"timestampLabel":"37:57","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And per the law, we may be required to do this until they're 22. Is that correct? Correct, yes. So I just kind of let you give the quick sum synopsis there. Yeah, absolutely. I shared with you guys today three different documents. One of those is the Special Education Excess Cost Funding Manual, SEEK Funding Manual. And so it does go through and talk about all of the requirements that we must provide to students and families when we fall into this type of financial","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2307-90","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2307,"timestampLabel":"38:27","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I'm going to say that the state calls it a burden. So what this says is that if we are over three times the state average of what a student would typically receive in Indiana, then it falls under excess cost. So that allows us then to submit an application to be able to reimburse on those excess cost. So for both of the students that I'm asking you to look at agreements with tonight, we are definitely over the three times there. And as Christine pointed out,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2337-91","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2337,"timestampLabel":"38:57","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Exhibit A in this contract does break that down, so you can see, it's the very last page in that contract, you can see how much Heritage, for instance, charges on a daily rate to provide special education services, how much they charge to provide room and board, and then any therapeutic services that are determined as a need for that student as well. We are required to exhaust all funds in terms of what we can provide for those students, so for instance,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2367-92","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2367,"timestampLabel":"39:27","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- amount that we receive on ADM for each of these students, we go to pay for our deductible on these kiddos, which is around $30,000. That is actually determined by the Indiana Department of Education, how much we are required to spend out of pocket before SEEK, as long as we're approved, begins picking up reimbursements for that. We also will take the special education funds that we receive for each of these students for their disabilities, and we will apply that","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2397-93","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2397,"timestampLabel":"39:57","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- towards the deductibles as well. The additional funds for us, we will take out of Medicaid to be able to pay for these students at the level that we're required to pay. And then I can't stress this enough with the hope that SEEK funds will pick up the rest of that. If SEEK funds does not have enough in that fund to pay for it, then it goes back to the school. It does. Okay. It does. And that will be","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-241-10","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":241,"timestampLabel":"4:01","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- During that time, we'll also put out a notice. This would be a bond issuance through your building corporation. That's a 30-day notice, and because of the way that your meetings run and the newspaper runs, we would be back at your September board meeting, and we'd also have the building corporation meet probably just before your meeting to consider an amendment to your existing lease with the building corporation. This would be a building corporation bond.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2423-94","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2423,"timestampLabel":"40:23","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- A situation where SEEK can say we can reimburse 100%, they can also come back at any point in time and say we can reimburse up to a certain percentage. That is not anything that we have any control over. We will make sure that the applications we submit are thorough. We'll make sure that we have justification and need","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2446-95","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2446,"timestampLabel":"40:46","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- put in there in writing for every single one of these students. What will be a little bit different about the applications for SEEK this year than what we did last year. These are considered re-applications, so we do work really closely with the","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2461-96","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2461,"timestampLabel":"41:01","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- offsite residential placement facilities in terms of providing documentation that these students are gaining in terms of academics. That's important. If we see that they're not gaining academically, if they're not making behavioral gains or whatever the situation might be, then as a case conference committee, that's where we have to come back to the table and say, is this the appropriate placement for this student? And so we're keeping a close eye on that.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2491-97","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2491,"timestampLabel":"41:31","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- That'll be a piece that we'll report on in those applications. And these are two students that live in our school district. Yes, they are two students that live in our school district that have siblings who attend our schools on a daily basis, two families that I've known for a long time that really work well with us and thankfully trust us to make good decisions for their kids. You know these services?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2519-98","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2519,"timestampLabel":"41:59","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- can be expensive, but my wife's a teacher and on her wall she has fair is not everybody getting the same thing. It's everybody getting what they need to succeed. That's absolutely the agreement that we have with every family and it's also what we pledge to provide as a public school system for every single one of our students that walk through the door. Which is named by all public schools, including public charter schools. That is correct. Okay, perfect.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2550-99","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2550,"timestampLabel":"42:30","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Thank you. You're welcome. Any further discussion? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. And now we'll look for the agreement with the Judge Rottenberg Educational Center. So this is a very similar agreement for another student. This student is receiving his or her special education services in Massachusetts.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2575-100","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2575,"timestampLabel":"42:55","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- We're asking you to approve this agreement for this student on the same basis, same outline, just like we talked about previously, this organization has a little bit different fee schedule, which makes sense. But ultimately, we would be looking at 250 to $300,000 as an agreement for the student special education services out of state at this facility.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2606-101","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2606,"timestampLabel":"43:26","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And just like the previous agreement, we will be submitting a seek application for this kiddo as well. And hoping that the state has those funds available to be able to reimburse us 100%. I'll move approval of the judgment for educational center agreement. Any discussion? The board packet does include the specific amounts for this one.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2636-102","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2636,"timestampLabel":"43:56","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- It will not right now, Larry. The reason for that is that will be determined once we finish the IEP and determine what those services look like for that student. So it would depend.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2649-103","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2649,"timestampLabel":"44:09","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- on that student's disability, it would depend on a lot of different pieces there. So once we have that, then we can go ahead and get the contract written. So this is just simply the agreement with both of these facilities. Once we have the IEP, we go ahead and we start the contract with them. And then we can bring that back before the board so you can see those actual amounts. But keep in mind with IEPs, those are completely flexible. They can change at any point in time. If we see a change in services that are needed, we come together.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-265-11","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":265,"timestampLabel":"4:25","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Then we would be back in October to authorize the issuance of bonds. There's a couple of additional public hearings there just to make sure the public has a chance to comment. And then we would be in a position to close potentially in mid-November. I think Jerry would work with Stiefel to kind of determine the best time when you need funds, if it's best to wait till closer to the end of the year or when it's best to price. So with that, I'll turn it back over to you, Mr. President.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2679-104","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2679,"timestampLabel":"44:39","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- almost immediately to look at those services and they can change on a dime. That's a good thing. That's what we want to happen because we want to make sure that we're providing what those students need even if they're in Massachusetts or they're in Utah. So we will show you the initial contract and we'll ask you at that point in time to understand and to make sure that we have the flexibility to be able to change that as needed. Thank you. You're welcome.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2708-105","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2708,"timestampLabel":"45:08","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- to consider this a not to exceed 300,000. Well, and it sounds like it'll come back to you with the exact amounts. But yeah, I would say that. OK. All right. Any further discussion? Maybe at the end of the year. I know Ms. Barrett said we were able to seek money this past year. Yes, we have been. Just make sure that we continue to get that. And we make sure we got across our T's and dot our I's,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2737-106","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2737,"timestampLabel":"45:37","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Did we have two cases last year as well? Yes, and these are the exact same two students who have been placed since that time. So no new students. These are the same ones. What you have approved are their agreements for the upcoming school year. So July 1 to June 30 is the contract date on those. Thank you. The agreement will have to be approved every year. Yes.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2761-107","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2761,"timestampLabel":"46:01","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- The agreement allows us to apply for the seek funding. Then we'll move forward with the IEPs. All of that is sent to these organizations. The contracts are written up, and then we bring those back to you. Anything further? We pay upfront, as far as you're right, for the whole year. And then we get the money later. So that's a great question. So we will pay upfront our deductible.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2786-108","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2786,"timestampLabel":"46:26","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Now, we will be charged, so we'll receive an invoice from each organization over the course of the year.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2793-109","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2793,"timestampLabel":"46:33","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I don't know if that's monthly or quarterly. I would have to look at that and see. What we do then is we go ahead and pay that and then we turn around and we apply for a reimbursement through SEEK. So Debbie Tate takes care of all of those reimbursements. As far as the deductible that we would pay on each one of these students, we pay that upfront and then that money comes back to us in terms of our ADM count, in terms of our Part B grant when that's dispersed, December count with our","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2823-110","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2823,"timestampLabel":"47:03","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- education students and then Medicaid billing throughout the year. So we would see that come back on a rolling basis. All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Now we look for at the furniture bids for the high school and junior high school. Dr. Sanders. Thank you Mr. Kerr.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2849-111","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2849,"timestampLabel":"47:29","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I am recommending the board approve the purchase of additional classroom furniture for Edgewood Junior High School and Edgewood High School. Both schools have been working on us to get the new furniture for a while and we've heard them and we agree that this furniture is,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2871-112","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2871,"timestampLabel":"47:51","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- It's well overdue to be replaced. It's well over 20 years old. And so we will be paying for this furniture out of the 2022 general obligation bond. The quotes are already competitively bid through the co-op and meets procurement policies and rules. The total cost of the furniture for the junior high, and it's the same cost for both schools, 158,000.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2899-113","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2899,"timestampLabel":"48:19","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- $279 and 80 cents. And the new furniture will be installed over fall break vacation. The furniture bids. Discussion. I like the more flexible design, the separated desk and chair that I see. I know I had","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2926-114","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2926,"timestampLabel":"48:46","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- within the last 20 years, if you say, a number of desks that were the pieces, the bottom storage racks were broken and it was hard to keep them looking good and they were dangerous at times. So no, I like this. Yes, I saw the chairs first and I thought that was like student chairs. It's like, oh my gosh. Yeah, I saw the same thing. But that's teacher chairs. I understand. OK.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2956-115","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2956,"timestampLabel":"49:16","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Anything further? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Now we're going to look at purchasing staff laptops and for that we have our tech director Rick Ratton. Evening everybody. So it's that time of year, our time when we do capital replacement. It's been five years since we came to you and got the original laptops for the staff.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-296-12","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":296,"timestampLabel":"4:56","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And now we'll hear from Dr. Sanders about the process of determining the scope of the project and the need for the project. And he'll also provide a general description of the project. Mr. McClellan did a pretty good job at that and how it addresses the school, community, and student needs. So as Jacob mentioned, we have a number","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-2982-116","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":2982,"timestampLabel":"49:42","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Great time. Looking forward to seeing some new laptops for our staff and everybody around here. So we did do bid proposals. We only received two back. We sent out six, but only two actually replied. One was Trafera, a new company that we just started working with about a year ago, and they've been competitively bidding on some of our other stuff, but this time they did not","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-30-1","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":30,"timestampLabel":"0:30","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And if you would be interested in speaking at the hearing this evening, we would ask that you sign in and you would be, we'll go through the rules of that if anybody signs in. So at this point, I'd like to ask that Jacob McClellan from Bo's McKinney and Evans explain the purpose of this hearing. He's our public counsel.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3006-117","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3006,"timestampLabel":"50:06","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- come in at the lowest price. We have been using Paragon Micro for the last purchase, and they again won this year's process of elimination. About $3,000 difference, but they were both very high-end laptops, one's with Lenovo brand and one was a Dell brand, so we've been looking at both, both area.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3024-118","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3024,"timestampLabel":"50:24","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- So I'm asking for your approval tonight to approve that we move forward with the purchase of Dell laptops from Paradigm Micro for a total of $341,996. Move approval of the staff laptop purchase. I'll second. Moved and second. Any discussions? Does that take care of whole staff? It takes care of 400 staff members. Is there any residual value on the","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3053-119","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3053,"timestampLabel":"50:53","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- computers that we're replacing? So on the residue, the runs we're going to keep that are still in good shape and have not been stickered to death, we're going to repurpose those into some of the classrooms that have some old workstations that really do need to be removed and updated. So we're going to repurpose them. We have to be careful because our licensing with Microsoft, we have to stay within a certain range. And so some of them we won't be able to actually reuse. We'll have to, we'll try to get some money out of them.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3082-120","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3082,"timestampLabel":"51:22","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- More than likely 20, $30 is all we seem to be getting for refurbished equipment. Yeah, I was just kind of curious. When do you think they'll be ready to roll? We probably won't see these until somewhere October, November, just because of the way that orders have been going and the tariffs and everything. And then we'll have to start doing the rollout to all the individual teachers. So by the time the furniture comes in?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3109-121","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3109,"timestampLabel":"51:49","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Approximately, we also have a lot of other stuff coming around. We just don't have time to even start that process. We have already received the 900 laptops for the high school, or excuse me, Chromebooks for the high school students, and we're already getting those into the students' hands. We're trying to get those out early, because it's a lot of processing to do. Right. But from time to time, the teachers can see them as Christmas presents, so. That's what I'm looking at. I thought we'd just get Dr. Sanders to dress up as Santa Claus, and he can deliver a few of them.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3138-122","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3138,"timestampLabel":"52:18","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Make it a little happy, happy end of year season. Yeah. Is that part of collective bargaining? No, I'm joking. I'm joking. But it's something that we definitely need in this time. Five years is about the maximum we can see out of all the devices. Is that from a rolling fund or part of bonds? We got a bond. That's what I thought. Any further discussion? All those in favor say aye.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3168-123","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3168,"timestampLabel":"52:48","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Now we have consideration to approve agreement with IU for DBT informed training and school counselors and they're for Barrett.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3182-124","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3182,"timestampLabel":"53:02","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- That agreement is actually being paid for out of our SMART grant. That's one of our federal grants for mental health. We have in excess carryover funds of about $500,000, and this grant is very specific about how it can be spent. This is a type of training. It's a therapeutic approach, and it will be a virtual training given by the same IU instructors that we currently work with in partnership of the SMART grant.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3211-125","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3211,"timestampLabel":"53:31","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- So we're asking you to approve this. This training probably won't take place until spring, and I'll be bringing a contract back to you after the agreement has been approved for the contract also to be approved. I'll move the bill. I second. Moved and second. Any discussion? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. In consideration to approve the Northwestern University Medical","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-322-13","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":322,"timestampLabel":"5:22","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- projects that we have established for these bond hearings. We've gone through","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3240-126","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3240,"timestampLabel":"54:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- social service service agreement. This agreement also same terms and with a smart grant and what we're looking at here our counselors","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3252-127","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3252,"timestampLabel":"54:12","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- have learned about a new therapeutic approach that is being researched out at Northwestern University. This is a single session consultation, so we're looking at those students who aren't necessarily needing long-term therapy, long-term counseling. This approach is more kind of a","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3273-128","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3273,"timestampLabel":"54:33","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- fly by the seat of your pants, get the kids back in class sort of approach. And it's one that we think will definitely come in beneficial to the students in terms of maybe being proactive in some of the situations that we have going on versus being reactive","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3293-129","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3293,"timestampLabel":"54:53","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And possibly taking more time out of classes for them to receive those therapies. So this is again with Northwestern University and coming out of those carryover funds with the smart grant And is this one where the contract will come later as well I am","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3317-130","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/15/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14775","timestampSeconds":3317,"timestampLabel":"55:17","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I believe that this agreement has all of the terms and there was an amendment. Amendment isn't the correct term. There was an appendix to it that had all of the","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14775-tx-3330-131","meetingDate":"2025-07-15","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7