ame":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- But if there's anything I'm not allowed to answer tonight, Jake will be back here at the next Tuesday meeting. Jake probably did not mention that he was sending someone that graduated from the rival Hohen Valley a couple decades ago, so please don't hold that against me. And I don't know your mom and dad. You probably do know my mom and dad. Yeah, I thought we had said we'll knock on your next door. Recently retired Dr. Cochran, that's right. Yeah, right on. Well, Pursuit to Indiana Code 6-1.1-20-3.5, a school corporation must hold two public hearings","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-147-5","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":147,"timestampLabel":"2:27","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and adopt a resolution preliminary determining to issue bonds or enter into a lease for a project that has a total project costs in excess of the non-controlled project threshold of $1 million. These public hearings and the adoption of the resolution that will be considered at the next meeting are the very beginning of this entire legal process for this project. The resolutions themselves establish the maximum financial terms for the proposed project.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-172-6","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":172,"timestampLabel":"2:52","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- For the record, all of the statutorily required information is located on that table at the entrance of the meeting, as required by statute. If proceeding forward, this project will be financed by an issuance of bonds pursuant to the school's building corporation's existing indenture and lease. There will be a supplement to the indenture and an amendment to the lease. Those will be drafted and circulated and approved as part of the overall authorization process. Our current timeline has us working through all of the legal processes through","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-202-7","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":202,"timestampLabel":"3:22","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- mid-October, anticipating selling the bonds in early November and then closing on the bonds in late November. As mentioned, this is the very first step in the overall legal process. There is no action required by the board tonight, only just to hold this public hearing. And if there are any questions or comments, please hesitate to ask. Thank you very much. And we will now hear from Dr. Sanders.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-230-8","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":230,"timestampLabel":"3:50","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- about the process of determining the scope of the project and the need for this project? Certainly. So the scope of the project developed out of a comprehensive effort to determine the most prioritized needs across the Edgewood School's campus. We used the following sources. In 2022, we had a facility assessment done by","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-254-9","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":254,"timestampLabel":"4:14","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Lancer architect firm in 2024, just last fall. We also had a demographic study done by McKimmon's demographic and research. And then most recently we've had a number of work sessions where we've, as you know, we invited teachers, administrators,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-281-10","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":281,"timestampLabel":"4:41","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- We had our athletic director here, teachers and coaches from the performing arts, maintenance. We met with skillman construction managers and a Lancer architecture to determine what our needs would be. The project will serve to provide a better educational opportunity for Edgewood students across the campus by providing elements of effective","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-30-1","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":30,"timestampLabel":"0:30","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Just pause for a moment with all the tragedy in Texas. So many young school aged kids have passed, and so we'll just take a couple seconds. Okay.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-310-11","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":310,"timestampLabel":"5:10","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and positive educational environment, which includes students and staff must feel safe, students and staff must feel positive about their learning environment, students and staff must, or students must be actively engaged in the educational process. As a result, the project consists of the construction and equipping of renovations, improvements and additions to","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-338-12","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":338,"timestampLabel":"5:38","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Edgewood High School including, but not limited to, roof replacement, repair, and renovations, and solar installation. B, band choir expansion, upgrades, improvements, and renovations. C, constructing and equipping additional classrooms. D, constructing and equipping biomedical training classrooms. E, installation of turf to the baseball field.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-366-13","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":366,"timestampLabel":"6:06","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- F, installation of turf and other improvements and upgrades to the softball field. G, technology, office, storage, and workspace upgrades, replacements, and equipping. H, parking and asphalt repair, upgrades and replacements. I, tennis court repairs and renovations. And J, other related renovations, improvements, and upgrades to permit such","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-394-14","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":394,"timestampLabel":"6:34","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- buildings to be utilized for school purposes. Also, the construction of equipping of renovations, improvements, and additions to Edgewood Junior High School, including but not limited to roof replacement, repair, and renovations, and solar installation. B, banquire expansion upgrades, improvements, and renovations. C, constructing and equipping additional classrooms.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-423-15","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":423,"timestampLabel":"7:03","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- D, replacement of bleachers, E, parking and asphalt repair, upgrades and replacements, F, tennis court repairs and renovations, and G, other related renovations, improvements, upgrades to permit such buildings to be utilized for school purposes. Also, the construction and equipping of renovations, improvements, and additions to Edgewood Primary School","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-450-16","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":450,"timestampLabel":"7:30","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and Edgewood Intermediate School, including but not limited to A, roof replacement, repair and renovations and solar installation, B, playground expansion, improvements and renovations, C, asphalt patching, resurfacing and additional parking, D, other related renovations, improvements and upgrades to permit such buildings to be utilized for school purposes and","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-478-17","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":478,"timestampLabel":"7:58","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- for other related renovations, upgrades, improvements, repairs, replacements, and equipping by the school corporation at its facilities. And as you know, we often put there are more needs than there is money. So we obviously would not be able to do all these projects, but these are just kind of represent the most important needs across our campus.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-510-18","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":510,"timestampLabel":"8:30","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Now we will hear from Stiefel, and they are our underwriter, and they're going to explain how the proposed project will be financed, as well as information about the effect on the typical property taxpayer.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-524-19","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":524,"timestampLabel":"8:44","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Good evening, everybody. Thanks for having us here. So yeah, you guys, I think, have in front of you a hard copy. I'll just kind of walk through the different slides. Feel free to ask me questions. So on the first slide, this represents all of your current outstanding debt and the annual payments for each one of the individual six bond issues that you guys currently have outstanding.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-550-20","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":550,"timestampLabel":"9:10","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- On the second page in orange, we have layered in the proposed $40 million project as a potential 2025 approval. And so you can see after layering those in,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-564-21","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":564,"timestampLabel":"9:24","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- what the annual, proposed annual payments would potentially look like. You know, more than likely with a project this big, you're probably going to do it in multiple issues, you know, and that does help some of this picture as we move forward. And the plan is, as of right now, to keep your tax rate or your tax levy flat throughout the project, so then that would not be an increase to the taxpayer from this particular project, okay?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-594-22","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":594,"timestampLabel":"9:54","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And if we go to the last slide, I'm just going to read through some of what we call the legal parameters. I'll just kind of look at some of these. So the max par amount of the bonds being the $40 million, it will go out with a maturity of 20 years. Maximum interest rate right now in what we're running is around 7%. I can tell you today,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-615-23","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":615,"timestampLabel":"10:15","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Municipal bonds issued today are probably in the four and a half to four point three percent range. But we do use a conservative seven percent running your numbers. So estimated interest expense at the seven percent would be the forty seven million fifty two thousand. The max annual payment that we have in the parameters would be seven million dollars. So that would bring the maximum total payments to just over eighty seven million.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-64-2","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":64,"timestampLabel":"1:04","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- So I'd like to welcome all of you from the public to the meeting. This is our preliminary determination meeting. And so hopefully, we've got cats here, so this is being live streamed. And we are holding this preliminary hearing on a proposed project. If any do come and want to speak, they'll need to sign in.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-641-24","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":641,"timestampLabel":"10:41","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- The 2024 pay 25 debt service levy is 9.8 million and the 24 pay 25 debt service tax rate is 65 cents. That's just your current levy and 25 for debt and your current tax rate in the debt service fund. So as you can see, our plan is to keep the pay 26 levy around the same 9.8 million.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-663-25","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":663,"timestampLabel":"11:03","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Tax rate itself could go up a little bit if assessed value drops, but the levy is what reflects what the taxpayer is actually paying on, not the rate. Okay, so the plan is to keep that flat. Max annual payments as a percent of NAV are 6.43 percent, and your direct and overlapping debt as a percent of NAV is 8.02 percent. So, any questions with any of that?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-692-26","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":692,"timestampLabel":"11:32","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Net assessed value. Thank you. Yep. I always forget that one. In the debt service rate, we can't go over 70 cents as the new starting when? That starts in 2026. OK. And then next year. When Matt was here, Shoemaker, he was going to run one of these 30 million also just for us to look at. At 30? At 30. Yeah. Agreed. We can get that to Jared. Agreed. We're going to look at one just for comparison. Just to see what it looked like. OK.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-721-27","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":721,"timestampLabel":"12:01","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I would like to see that too. Okay. Okay. This is, I know this is a starting point. Yeah. Okay. Yeah. Cause you know, you can see there, you're probably looking at, you were approaching the 70 at the 0.68 cents. Yeah. At 40 million. Yeah. 40. Correct. And it's 7%. I mean, at the 7%. Yep. That'll all bring it down. Also doing it in multiple issuances. If we do it in two or three, that also makes that tax rate come down. Correct.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-752-28","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":752,"timestampLabel":"12:32","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Absolutely the goal would be to keep you guys under the 70 cents. No referendum. No referendum. Got it. All right. We're good. All right. Now is the time that we would open this hearing up for public comments. Doesn't look like we have anybody that's commenting. So therefore, I will close the public hearing.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-782-29","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":782,"timestampLabel":"13:02","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- We appreciate everyone for your time and incoming this evening. Thank you to Katz for keeping us going. Were you able to pick us up okay with all the drums? Awesome. Awesome. I just want to know if they're here. I thought I'd better check on that. Okay. So this meeting is adjourned, so thank you all very much.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14750-tx-94-3","meetingDate":"2025-07-08","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 7/8/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14750","timestampSeconds":94,"timestampLabel":"1:34","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I do want to make note that the notice of this preliminary determination hearing was published as legally required. And at this time, I will ask that Colin Cochran from Bowes, McKinney & Evans explain the purpose of this hearing. Good evening, members of the board. Colin Cochran with Bowes, McKinney & Evans. I am filling in for my colleague, Jake McClellan.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-0-0","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":0,"timestampLabel":"0:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Next meeting to order, please stand for the Pledge of Allegiance. I pledge allegiance to the flag of the United States of America, and to the republic for which it stands, one nation under God, indivisible, with liberty and justice for all. Thank you all. Please be seated. And welcome to the June 2025 school board meeting, just a couple of weeks away from having a half of a year going already.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1021-37","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1021,"timestampLabel":"17:01","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- We've got the exterior pretty well done. You can see the green metal panels. My sense is probably a lot of you have seen that in person. But rather than go through all the little items on last 60 and next 60, if it's all right with you all, I'd kinda like to just talk about what we're really driving on. The thing we need to get, and as we go through it, you'll see some pictures of the kitchen. We're really pushing on the kitchen.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1051-38","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1051,"timestampLabel":"17:31","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- The reason we're doing that is we need to get a Board of Health inspection before it can be used and we also need to have Vicki, right, get it stocked and ready to go. So right now we have the kitchen equipment installed and Matt you might flip another couple pages.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1076-39","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1076,"timestampLabel":"17:56","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- So all the kitchen equipment's on site. It's installed. We're doing just some minor stuff and some cleanup We're doing cleanup this week What we want to do is the first week of July get the Board of Health in there to look at it It's not unusual for them to have a few things to to touch up and that would give us a couple weeks to do that and we're hoping by","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-110-4","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":110,"timestampLabel":"1:50","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Then we have personnel, resignations, retirements, non-renewals, leaves and terminations. That is C, one through 35. And D, personnel appointments and transfers, one through 57. And then we have out-of-state and overnight field trips, E, one through seven. And these are all of the normal high school and junior high","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1106-40","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1106,"timestampLabel":"18:26","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- no later than July 21st to have that where it can be stocked and start using it. And again, if we do that the first week of July, that would give us three weeks to make that happen. We're hitting flooring real hard next week. And we ought to have a lot of the administration in those type of areas. Ceiling pads, we're dropping in ceiling pads.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1136-41","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1136,"timestampLabel":"18:56","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Right now, jump to the administration and the clinic. I believe we've got map furniture coming on July 15th, if I'm correct on that. Yeah, furniture delivery install, yeah. So what our goal is to have the administration and clinic set up by July 21st, and I'm getting way off our PowerPoint here. But if we have that by July 21st,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1166-42","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1166,"timestampLabel":"19:26","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- set up, then Heather and her staff can get in there and get themselves going. And again, as I think everybody's aware, we're really pushing the early childhood. We've condensed it to a pretty short window and I think we're gonna make it. Teachers, we're saying they're gonna be in there on the 28th and we'll be able to set up their classrooms. That only really gives them one week","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1197-43","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1197,"timestampLabel":"19:57","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- but we need to get it done and get cleaned before they move in. Paving will be done yet this month, but a lot of the landscape, and we're putting sod in up next to the building. So from the parking lot, it's gonna look done, because we'll have sod up there. But the fall planting season doesn't really start","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1225-44","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1225,"timestampLabel":"20:25","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- until I think it's August 15th. So any turf out in the swale or around the north side of the building where it's seeded, that'll get seeded probably that first couple, or second couple weeks of August. And you're really not gonna see the turf coming up until September, October. What else have we got? Okay. And then the other thing that's,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1255-45","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1255,"timestampLabel":"20:55","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- that we're pushing is the playground. What we want to do is get all the paving and all that kind of stuff done so they can get around the north side of the building. And again, I'm way off of the program here. But the playground should be installed early July. They're waiting for a couple of events for that. And then they'll move into that.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1284-46","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1284,"timestampLabel":"21:24","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Again, not to spend a lot of time on this piece, but I don't know if you want to look at some of the pretty pictures we have, if we could do that. And I guess with that, are there any questions on the early childhood? At this point, we feel pretty good about it. We're at the point where","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1311-47","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1311,"timestampLabel":"21:51","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Weather really doesn't impact us much. We've got, there are five mechanical units, rooftop units that do the air conditioning for the building. We've got three of them running right now, so that whole classroom wing is under condition. Now, what that means is, the units are running. We don't have the controls, the computer controls up and running yet.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1341-48","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1341,"timestampLabel":"22:21","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- So they just manually turn it on and off as they need it. It's important to have that done because that casework is subject to humidity as are the ceilings. So we've got that all under control. On the west side of the building, what we're calling unit A, the two units are not running yet, but they should be running next week. So right now we're running,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1371-49","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1371,"timestampLabel":"22:51","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- portable dehumidification in there. You guys sitting on, I was up here Saturday and there were, there was probably 15 people that were working Saturday. Are you working on Sundays too? I'm not. You're not. I know I didn't, I haven't seen you ever on a weekend, but I don't, I was just, they were getting after 40 yard on Saturday. I tell you what, Dale is pushing them like crazy. It's making it happen. All right.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-140-5","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":140,"timestampLabel":"2:20","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- athletic camps, so that's what those are. So do we have a motion? I move approval. Good and seconded. Any discussion? All those in favor? Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Dr. Sanders. Yes, we have, obviously if you looked at the agenda, we have a long list of new teachers","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1401-50","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1401,"timestampLabel":"23:21","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Yeah, they have, yeah. There's not a whole lot of days between now and the first week. Anyway, I thought that was more valuable than running piece by piece. High school, Matt, you might flip into that, obviously. We're working on the outside. You can see our little red brick pier, which I think the next slide is a close-up of that.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1431-51","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1431,"timestampLabel":"23:51","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Site work We've not been doing a lot of site work the last 60 days We're working on the grease interceptor on the building And I kind of let you guys look at that rather than go through it item by item There's our red brick pier on the south side of the building and","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1460-52","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1460,"timestampLabel":"24:20","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- That kind of works with the red brick on the north side of your building to try to tie it all together. That looks a little green in the slide. But you can see the, even though they're both green, the color of the concrete panels kind of work with the color of the limestone. And with that red separating them, I think it makes it work. The next 30 days we'll complete the metal panels.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1490-53","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1490,"timestampLabel":"24:50","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- We're gonna install the athletic equipment. And let me look at my notes here. We're starting to install the equipment now. We need to get the air conditioning going before we do the floor, which should be in the next couple of weeks. But the floor will go in in late to July. Now, just a reminder that the field house","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1520-54","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1520,"timestampLabel":"25:20","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Was never scheduled to be done by by fall term We've got that scheduled in our as bid schedule as being done in September and we might beat that We might be able to get it done sometime in August no promises, but we're pushing toward that Kitchen there's the chaos of the kitchen a whole lot of block work that that used to be your auxiliary gym and","transcri