stion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1809-64","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1809,"timestampLabel":"30:09","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- the media center and then there's a classroom right off of the media center. So that on the left is the media center, on the right is that classroom. They're moving along nicely and should be ready by the time school starts. And with that, anything else on the intermediate school? I know I've gotten off the track of the PowerPoint,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1836-65","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1836,"timestampLabel":"30:36","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Again, if Matt can get that to you, you can look at it at your leisure and it'll get down more to the nitty gritty. But right now, intermediate school looks very good. Primary school, we're trying to get all the toilet rooms done. We'll have them all done at least except one. And the early childhood looks good.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1864-66","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1864,"timestampLabel":"31:04","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- The turf and grass and bushes won't be done. The other thing we're looking at, I think, is signage. We should have the building signage, the interior room signage. If we have to put temporary signage up, we will. Just as a reminder, the board's taking a tour of the construction projects tomorrow night. Meet here at 530. That's exciting.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1894-67","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1894,"timestampLabel":"31:34","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- What's that big old hole when I came in and I parked up by the baseball field and because it was all gated off, what's that big hole for between the activity center and are they putting pipes still or is they going to pave it? You know, I didn't see the hole. What we're talking about by the field house area? Yes, like I get my directions between the field house. Probably the grease interceptors and or the drainage. They're probably connecting drainage. I just don't think it will repave all. I assume it's going to have to be repaved. Oh, yeah, it's got to be repaved. One thing.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1923-68","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1923,"timestampLabel":"32:03","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and I'm kind of looking at Matt, but I think there's a little discussion on whether we had talked about reducing that with the sidewalk in order to make the road a little wider. In order to do that, we've got to procure some additional storm structures. I don't know if there's- Just waiting on engineer on that. We're waiting on the engineer on that.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-194-7","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":194,"timestampLabel":"3:14","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- So I'll introduce both of us. Yes. Well, we are very happy to share tonight our new assistant principal at Edgewood Primary School, Alisa Van Dusen. And she comes with a very well-rounded background. She's had 14 years in the classroom, and many of those years have been in first and second grade with a touch of fifth grade. So that's good. And then she's been a Title I reading specialist for the last few years.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1951-69","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1951,"timestampLabel":"32:31","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- if we go ahead with it per the original plans, the structures are already in and they can just get the sidewalks in and get it paved. So I'm not real sure, Matt, where we are with that. Still looking to widen. Yeah, just trying to get a clarification of whether or not it's a different type of grate that would make the intersection a little wider and not affect the storm structure. So they're supposed to be giving us an answer on that.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-1979-70","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":1979,"timestampLabel":"32:59","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- we know how to proceed with it so they can make sure that things stay on time. So that's still a four way stop right there? Yeah, three way stop. Yeah, that's right there, yeah. Okay, all right. But what, until we get those, if we go forward and narrow the sidewalk and widen the street, then we will have to have new storm structures and the structures, the manhole essentially. Right, right.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2007-71","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2007,"timestampLabel":"33:27","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and it will take a few weeks to get those structures. So we're trying to move forward with the paving in the next several weeks, but if we have to change the structures, that'll, there'll be some things on the west side of the parking lot that won't be done concurrently with the rest of the paving. Okay. Over.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2035-72","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2035,"timestampLabel":"33:55","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Thank you very much, Martin. Appreciate your help and looking forward to seeing you tomorrow. I think you'll see, I'm sorry, I think you'll see Dale tomorrow. Well, I said see it. Yeah, yeah. You don't want to come back for another evening? You don't want to come back for another evening? I don't know, are we back here on Thursday? Friday, you're here Friday morning. Friday.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2067-73","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2067,"timestampLabel":"34:27","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Appreciate it. Thanks Martin. Thank you. Thanks Martin Now as we complete some projects, let's have a discussion about 2025 bonds timeline Mr. When you like to yeah, so I'll kind of just","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2091-74","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2091,"timestampLabel":"34:51","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- kind of queue up who's here and what we've been having discussions about possible projects. We've had multiple work sessions at this point to discuss some of the various needs of the school corporation, as well as look at kind of what our financial outlook is and what our possibilities are for this upcoming year and some of those projects. So here tonight is Matt Shoemaker from Stiefel who's been at the work session is presenting some of this information to you previously. So some of this,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2119-75","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2119,"timestampLabel":"35:19","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- All of it should be a review for you in that way, but he's gonna continue to touch on those things. And then again, just presenting in a board meeting so that people in the public can continue to see that information and we're making sure that we're putting that out there to everyone. And then Jacob McClellan from Boas McKinney or Bond Council is gonna talk through the proposed timeline and what that would look like and walk you through all those pieces. But I know you're all well versed in this, but that's who's here tonight. So we'll start with Matt Shoemaker from Stiefel.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2148-76","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2148,"timestampLabel":"35:48","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Good evening. Good to see you all again.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2153-77","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2153,"timestampLabel":"35:53","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I'll be brief tonight. I know we've been over some of this before, but this page looks at all of your outstanding debt as of today, color coded by issue. So all the payments stack on top of each other to show you what your annual payment is, not only in 2025, but moving forward all the way through 2042. Obviously, this has been done intentionally, always with an eye to the future to make sure as we're doing these projects, we're doing them under your financial goals.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2183-78","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2183,"timestampLabel":"36:23","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- 2025 you can see total payments are about 10 million just under 10 million dollars schedules drop in 26 27 in 2028 obviously that was intentional so that we can add on projects such as these and again hit hit hit the goals that you've set for so as we look at the next page so we have put in a potential 40 million dollar bond issue and","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-219-8","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":219,"timestampLabel":"3:39","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and an intervention coordinator, as well as an assistant to the principal. So she's got some solid experience. She's been in the building already. She's met a few teachers, and she's seen her new office. But now it's all been cleaned out. So the key is on my desk. Come and get it, and you can move in. You can move in tomorrow. And then we also are happy to have Maitland","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2209-79","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2209,"timestampLabel":"36:49","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- As of today, we've shown all of this being issued at once. We know that's not going to happen. Obviously these projects are most likely gonna take months and months, if not over the course of a couple years. But we've done it this way to be most conservative. If you issue everything at one time, you're gonna start paying interest on everything at one time. So this picture should be worst case scenario. As you guys decide exactly how and when you wanna do some of these projects, if you bring","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2239-80","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2239,"timestampLabel":"37:19","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- break this up into smaller bond issues over a period of time, that's going to make this chart look a lot better. You're not paying interest on everything right away, so you're saving some interest costs. Also, you can only pay these bonds back over a course of 20 years. So if you end up issuing these bonds, say, over the next two or three years, you get 20 years on each issue. So that can be extended out. All of this picture is going to look a lot better. The reason I've done it this way is simply to show you that you can keep your levy the same moving forward.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2269-81","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2269,"timestampLabel":"37:49","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- if you choose under any circumstance if you're talking about a $40 million bond issue. As we've talked about in the past, the tax rate is somewhat up in the air because we don't know the full effects of the new legislation. But what we do know is this can be structured so that the levy, the amount of property taxes we're asking taxpayers to pay, remains constant moving forward if that's what the school board administration decides to do. So I think my message is fairly simple in that we can do this under the worst circumstance","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2299-82","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2299,"timestampLabel":"38:19","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- However, you guys end up breaking this up is only going to make this look better. But in either scenario, if you want to keep those property tax dollars that levy the same moving forward, that can certainly be accomplished with the size of a project. Questions about any of this? Can you send a chart at 30 million, too? Oh, of course. Anything, yeah.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"au