ault of your own because of what the legislature did. Then you have that, if you have that authorization, you have the bill. Right. I mean, that's the... Yeah, and that authorization sticks. I mean, there are plenty of schools that will do this and they won't, they'll issue it over three, five, seven years. The timing and the amounts are totally up to the school board and the administration on how you want to do that. If we do it correct, if we do it correctly, then we won't have to do the referendum.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2495-89","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2495,"timestampLabel":"41:35","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- That is the ultimate goal, yes. Now, do they change the goalposts again? As of today, that is the goal, yes. So right now, we're looking at Friday, the meeting we talked about earlier that we're gonna have on Friday is actually taking some of the projects that we've prioritized and we've given them estimated costs. We wanna be much more precise in that","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-2522-90","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":2522,"timestampLabel":"42:02","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And then once we have that finished, then we'll come back to you. And then as a board, you'll be able to prioritize and say, well, these two projects need to be done sooner rather than later. And then we'll see how