n?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3096-111","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3096,"timestampLabel":"51:36","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. All right. Thank you very much. Thank you very much, guys. Thank you. Matt and Jake, I really appreciate you guys coming down and making everything so clear. I appreciate it. Thanks.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3132-112","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3132,"timestampLabel":"52:12","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I didn't want to do it necessarily at the beginning of the meeting because we had everybody here and it was such a joyous time. But I would like to take a moment to pause and stop and remember Cindy Bentley and her family. It was a very tragic loss. The driver in the other car actually","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3160-113","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3160,"timestampLabel":"52:40","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- someone that I had had as a student at Ivy Tech. So I knew both. She was Jasmine was St. John was in the other car and she was the administrative assistants at the proactive health clinic. So a lot of our folks know her. Yeah. Yeah. So it is a very sad time for them and their families and we just know it.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3189-114","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3189,"timestampLabel":"53:09","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- my prayers are with them, and that if we could just take a few moments of silence, I think we should. Okay. So,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3219-115","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3219,"timestampLabel":"53:39","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- No, we will go ahead. We have an informational item that is the revisions to policies 4162 and 8510, and this would be the first reading, and Dr. Sadler. Yeah, so we, as you mentioned, we have two policies that we're presenting to you tonight on first reading, and then at the July board meeting, we'll give you the opportunity to approve those","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3249-116","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":32