cats-14701-tx-3304-118","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3304,"timestampLabel":"55:04","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- kind of organizes and leads our corporation in areas of health and fitness. They felt like, once again, the language in policy 8510 should be revised to better align with the USDA smart snacks in school nutrition standards. And so we've revised those policies accordingly.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3333-119","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3333,"timestampLabel":"55:33","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Christine has reviewed them and this is first reading. So once again, we'll ask you to vote on this in July. Thank you. Now we will look at the administrator contract adjustments. Mr. Irwin. So this is for our preschool director. So with this upcoming year, we'll be doubling the size of the preschool. We'll be adding in the addition of the daycare.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3361-120","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3361,"timestampLabel":"56:01","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And she will have the over being overseeing the before and after care program, child care program as well. It's much more aligned with the duties and the things that she is focused on throughout the day and throughout the year. And with this, what we're trying to do is continue just to,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3379-121","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3379,"timestampLabel":"56:19","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- create a mold of rhyme and reason as to how we pay our administrators and how that's in alignment with other administrative positions and it being competitive as well. And so this brings this, the payment of our preschool director position in alignment with our AP positions at the elementary level as well. So some little bit more of equal footing as far as the level of responsibilities that are there. So that brings this into alignment. So it's an adjustment of this upcoming contract year, which would start July 1 through June 30","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3409-122","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3409,"timestampLabel":"56:49","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- of 2025 through 2026. So it's just an adjustment of that second year. The contract has been reviewed by Christine prior to it coming to you. The administrator contract adjustment. A second discussion. She is gonna have more on her plate this year. No question. She's been doing an outstanding job just getting prepared and planning for the opening of the new building.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3437-123","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3437,"timestampLabel":"57:17","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- She has been in on every detail and has been very meticulous in the way that she's planning and trying to get things set up and ready to go. So I applaud her for that. So it's still a 200 day contract. Same again, it's brought into alignment with that of an AP for the elementary buildings. Any further?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3467-124","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3467,"timestampLabel":"57:47","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Next is to approve status.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3474-125","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3474,"timestampLabel":"57:54","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- of the year-round classified employee agreements. Again, Mr. Irwin? Yeah, so this is a yearly piece. It's the status quo classified employee agreements for these six individuals. It's something that we do every year. So those are one-year agreements. So it's just to make sure that we renew their agreements prior to them expiring so that they're not walking into July on an expired contract. So this is, again, reviewed yearly by Christine prior to your approval. I move approval. I second.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3504-126","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3504,"timestampLabel":"58:24","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Any discussion? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carried. Now consideration to approve the PCS quote, nope, policy analytics agreement. Yeah, so the last time we worked with policy analytics was back in 2021. They did a tax-based study analysis for us.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3529-127","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3529,"timestampLabel":"58:49","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And so this is very similar in that way, but they're also gonna help us key in on some things that are very important with the changes as it relates to SEA 1. So again, having a firm understanding of our tax base and the direction that it's heading as well as the impact of the homeowners credit, that's an immediate impact on our budgets because it's gonna come off the top of our levy like a circuit breaker credit. And so they're gonna be able to give us much more accurate","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-354-13","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":354,"timestampLabel":"5:54","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- hired a new math teacher, new English teacher. I haven't hired this many teachers in a long time. And Shonda was just the first of a few home runs that we've hit for the high school. So really excited to have Shonda at the high school. She will be there. She missed Jackson, her oldest son, but she'll be there for Ryan. And I know that he's going to enjoy having mom around as well. So Shonda Klinger.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3555-128","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3555,"timestampLabel":"59:15","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- count as far as what to expect for that type of credit so that as we plan for budgets for cash flow projections when we're making decisions about staffing, we have more accurate detailed information to make decisions off of. So this is in alignment with the same reasons that we would do a demographic study or we would do a facility study assessment.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3572-129","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3572,"timestampLabel":"59:32","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- or all of those pieces, it brings good information to the board. They're one of the leader. They are the leader in this for around the state. They work with a lot of schools. And so this allows them to do it. It is a one-year agreement so that after one year, if we feel like we don't need to continue to do it, that's fine. But this will help us get some of that information so that we're better prepared as we make decisions in the near term. Small approval of the policy analytics agreement.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3602-130","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3602,"timestampLabel":"1:00:02","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Any discussion and that fees an annual cost, correct? Yeah, that is a cost of ten thousand five hundred dollars and it can be paid for either from the operations fund But I did check with Jacob McClellan from Bose because it is helping us with our analysis as it relates to bonding and some of those other projects we can include it in our Costs for issuance so that it doesn't come out of our operations fund It saves us that appropriation and that cash and operate operations, which is how I would advise to do that","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3632-131","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3632,"timestampLabel":"1:00:32","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and they give us more detailed information to Stiefel. Yes, yeah, so it's kind of a layer. Stiefel is more so on that side of advising us on bonds, bond parameters, all of those pieces. Policy Analytics is back in giving us a lot of information as it relates to our own tax base and what the parameters are of that as far as what to expect, AV growth, all of those other things, which helps make Stiefel's information that much more accurate as it relates to giving you information about those parameters. And they would be evaluating, for example, the TIF.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3662-132","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3662,"timestampLabel":"1:01:02","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Yeah, so they can look and help us with evaluating some impact of the TIF and some of those other pieces, which again is very appropriate for us at this time. Sure, thank you. Nothing further. All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. No consideration to approve the PCS quote for the junior high school. Yeah, so,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3687-133","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3687,"timestampLabel":"1:01:27","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- We have been looking for some space to house student support for students if they are removed from the classroom or they're waiting to see an administrator or they're hanging out there for the day working on work. Mr. Rensler gave up his office this year and moved to a different office so that they had a space for that. And so this would allow us to create some space that's not being well utilized at this point, which is in the teacher's lounge where a lot of teachers aren't using that right now.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3716-134","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3716,"timestampLabel":"1:01:56","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- would rather have a space where they can serve students. So it's putting a wall up in that space, cutting in a door, making sure all the appropriate HVAC","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3726-135","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3726,"timestampLabel":"1:02:06","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Fire alarm, strobe, all those things are there to help with that. And then also is solving a secondary issue, which is we have no direct access to the back of the bleachers in the main gym at the junior high. So our maintenance and custodial staff is having to kind of shimmy their way to the back to try to get in there to service or clean back there, which is not ideal in any aspect. So it takes care of that. They'll cut in a door and give direct access to the back of that for service and cleaning.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3755-136","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3755,"timestampLabel":"1:02:35","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- So we did put it out to three quoters.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3758-137","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3758,"timestampLabel":"1:02:38","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Only two people quoted. The low quote was provided by PCS. The total all in, if you take the alternates, which we would like to do, is $56,105, and it would be funded through some remaining funds of a bond back in 2010, which is an appropriate use of those funds. Checked with Jacob McClellan as far as what were the allowable uses of those remaining funds, and that's something that he said is an allowable use, so we would take it from that account, which has more than enough money to cover","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-378-14","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":378,"timestampLabel":"6:18","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I just put two and two together. Welcome aboard, glad you're here. And those boys are smart. So a little quick story about Jackson. We were already impressed with Jackson because of what he did with the coffee shop. And I couldn't make it to his open house. So Matt and I took him out to lunch.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3788-138","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3788,"timestampLabel":"1:03:08","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And so and also what you have in front of you is I printed off Christine wanted there to be like a standard AIA document like a short form document to go along with the quote Just because there was some renovation work going on in the building So we've been working with Ed surface and PCS to get that written out What I've given you is the latest version of that So what I'm asking for is for you guys to approve the quote and the agreement","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3813-139","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3813,"timestampLabel":"1:03:33","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- pending satisfactory language, which I expect to have soon, so that they can get this work done during the summer and hopefully have it ready before school year starts and that all of this is completed. So asking for approve that pending satisfactory language, the quote in the corresponding agreement. I'll second. Second, any discussion? Just curiosity, how big a space are we talking about?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3839-140","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3839,"timestampLabel":"1:03:59","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I don't recall the total square footage off the top of my head, but if you know where the teachers lounge access area is to the junior high, you walk in and you look to the left. So kind of where that little hallway is, that wall would go along where that hallway is. So it's still have that access hallway to get into the media center in that place, but it would wall that off. And then there'd be a door cut on the outside wall. That would be a direct access from the hallway into that room. Yeah, it's not, it's not, no, no, it's,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3869-141","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3869,"timestampLabel":"1:04:29","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And it's a much better utilization of that space than what it's being used for now. It's gonna be able to serve students, which is obviously a great thing. It'd be done this summer. So hopefully pending approval from you all, I'll be getting out that confirmation to them tomorrow so that they can get it scheduled because if not, if we had to wait till July, there's just no way that we would have the opportunity to get this work done. So we're really gonna be pushing on them to get this completed and finished before next school year starts.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3900-142","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3900,"timestampLabel":"1:05:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Mr. Siegel, does this make sense? This is what you guys want, right? Yeah, we're really limited in the office space and giving up an office to utilize it as high as this right now is a short-term fix on the long-term and something we really need. And for the number of teachers that utilize that space, we've got another space of mind that we can use. Is this like a 10 by 10 or a 20 by 20? I would say it's a whole pack.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3929-143","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3929,"timestampLabel":"1:05:29","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- 16 by 16, maybe 16 by 20, something like that. It's not a full classroom, but it's big enough to do. It would have to be for an extra suspension. Yeah, and it's, I mean, right now we're utilizing a space where we can only fit three students, four students maybe, or they're sitting on top of each other. Which, at the end of the break, they don't need to be sitting on top of each other anyway. But to go is not to have it, period.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3955-144","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3955,"timestampLabel":"1:05:55","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- We just need us we just need us we just need a space Did we have a motion, yes, was it contingent on the review by legal? Okay","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3982-145","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3982,"timestampLabel":"1:06:22","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Okay, there's nothing else all those in favor say aye aye opposed motion carries Thank you. And now we look at the renewal of the IU health athletic trainer agreement mr. Wang","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4011-146","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4011,"timestampLabel":"1:06:51","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Yeah, so last year was the first year that we had this agreement in place. This is a continuation of that agreement, obviously, but this is for a multi-year agreement. So not a whole lot of changes to the structure of the agreement. The initial price for this year is the exact same as what it was last year, but what they did was put a 3% escalator in it for each year just for it to keep up with cost of living and to keep that person's salary and benefits moving.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4038-147","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4038,"timestampLabel":"1:07:18","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Everything else is pretty close to the same. They made some slight tweaks to the marketing pieces that they would like in exchange for the sharing of costs for an athletic trainer. Looked into those some more. I don't think that it's gonna pose an issue to the school. It's not really any different than what we're doing now. And so this is just a partnership that we have with IU where they're helping to share in the cost of what it is to provide an athletic trainer to our teams.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4064-148","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4064,"timestampLabel":"1:07:44","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- At this point, we're very happy with where we're at with this, so I'm recommending your approval of this renewal. I'll move approval. I second. The cost of it? $43,000, and then next year it will go up by 3% each year thereafter. Any further? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Now permission to create the position of a certified","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-408-15","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":408,"timestampLabel":"6:48","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And he proceeds to tell me that he has this other business that he started on his own. It has to do with shoes. And I mean, it's just remarkable how he is able to use the technology to buy the shoes at a low price. And then he sells them. And that's his student-run business on his own. And then I just got to tell this because it's just so exciting.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4094-149","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4094,"timestampLabel":"1:08:14","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- occupational therapy assistant. Yes, so in the past we have had a contract with an outside company to provide the services of a certified occupational therapist assistant. We feel like we could possibly save the corporation some money by hiring this person directly. And so in order to do that, we have to create this position.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4122-150","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4122,"timestampLabel":"1:08:42","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And so we recommend your approval of that tonight. I'll second. You can second. Any discussion? Just curiosity, what do you anticipate that the cost would be for this person? Matt, do you know that?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4142-151","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4142,"timestampLabel":"1:09:02","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- You probably set the hourly rate somewhere in the mid 20s as far as what the going rate is. We're gonna continue to kind of look at what the analysis of what the going rate is for that. If we had to work with a contracting company, the markup on that is pretty extreme. And so we think that if we're able to find the right person, this would be a much better service to the kids and to the school corporation on every side of the spectrum.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4169-152","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4169,"timestampLabel":"1:09:29","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- This could be reimbursing some through maybe some Medicaid reimbursement. Yeah, I have to double check on on that on that, but I believe so. I think there's probably a little bit different reimbursement rates as it relates to different levels of professionals on licensing, but that would be something that if we're able to reimburse will continue to do that just like we build Medicaid services for those that are eligible to to bill. So they'll get benefits too. This is going to be a part time","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4200-153","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4200,"timestampLabel":"1:10:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And Next would be the creation of a position for a speech-language pathologist assistant Yes, so The purpose of this new position would really be to support our SLP's Kara glasscock who serves EPS and Justin Ross to who serves","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4228-154","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4228,"timestampLabel":"1:10:28","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- at the Edgewood Early Childhood Center. They've been doing a fantastic job trying to keep up with the growing demands, growing caseload. And so we feel though in order to support them, it would be really beneficial for the corporation to create this","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4251-155","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4251,"timestampLabel":"1:10:51","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- a speech and language pathologist assistant position so we can help take a little bit of the caseload off of these two fine educators. Last year we had had a, the board had approved an agreement for an outside,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-147