pSeconds":4534,"timestampLabel":"1:15:34","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Now consideration to approve the 2025 2026 before and after care handbook. Yeah, so bright bringing this to you because again with the change in the preschool again adding more opportunity for kids to have before and after care if they're in the preschool.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4554-167","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4554,"timestampLabel":"1:15:54","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And so this was something we've made several changes to it, felt like it was something that we needed to start bringing to you each year to review. The rates that are in the back end of it is something that you guys have already reviewed earlier in the year, just because we need to set those rates earlier as we are releasing information to families about that are looking into preschool or that are getting ready for kindergarten roundup or whatever that might be. So some of that stuff is some things that you've already seen before, but with some of these changes felt like it was necessary to start to bring that to you. And again,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4584-168","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4584,"timestampLabel":"1:16:24","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and will be under the direction of Heather Kenzik. She'll oversee the before and aftercare director. She'll still obviously work with the EPS and EIS administration to coordinate those services in those buildings, but she'll help with making sure that things are billing and all those other pieces are running the way that they should. So with that, asking for your approval on the before and aftercare handbook. Any discussion?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4613-169","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4613,"timestampLabel":"1:16:53","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. No consideration to approve the 2025-2026 student parent handbooks. Dr. Sanders. Yes, so I was just thinking about this. The handbooks are probably one of the most valuable documents that we have because it's such an effective way to communicate with parents and provide them with valuable information","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4640-170","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4640,"timestampLabel":"1:17:20","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- on procedures and other information that they need to know as parents. And so if you look at our handbooks, they're very well done. Our principals put a lot of time and energy into that. And every year, you kind of evaluate and think back on the past school year and different things that have come up. And then the principals think, well, we could better 