e. Opposed? Motion carries. I have consideration to approve power school section 504 software program contract. Mr. Erwin.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4719-173","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4719,"timestampLabel":"1:18:39","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Yeah, so this brings into alignment the state moved to power school being the provider of the new IEP platform as well. So it brings into alignment our section 504 plans in the IEP program being on the same platform, which makes it a lot easier for staff to make sure that we're administering the pieces that we need to for the students that get those services. So it was reviewed by Ferguson law. There was one change that needed to be made to it as it related to auto renewal.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4747-174","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4747,"timestampLabel":"1:19:07","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- That change has been made. So the agreement that you will be able to sign or approve at this point, Dr. Sanders will sign after pending your approval. It does have the auto renewal out of it, which is what Christine wanted to be out of it. They agreed to that change. So at this point, everything's good to go. So asking for your approval of that, please. I'll move approval. I'll second.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4771-175","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4771,"timestampLabel":"1:19:31","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- a set price contract, or is it? Yeah, so each year there's a set price. So year one, 25 to 26, is $5,822.50. Year two is $1,640.35. And then the years after, it has those in there as far as what those prices are. And then it has the subscription pieces that are in it. And it has the different layers in it as far as product services, training services. Training is $855.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4801-176","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4801,"timestampLabel":"1:20:01","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- so it lays out the different pieces that are in it. All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Okay, now we're to our friendly superintendent's report. You know, I just love this report tonight because so many times when I'm out and about, sometimes the public thinks that","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4830-177","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4830,"timestampLabel":"1:20:30","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- school corporations shut down during the summer.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4834-178","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4834,"timestampLabel":"1:20:34","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And I just wanted to give a report tonight to demonstrate that really our campus never sleeps. It's maybe moratorium week. It slows down a little bit. So our wonderful nutrition department is always on the move. As you know, they're providing free breakfast and lunch to students participating in summer school. We have the summer","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4860-179","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4860,"timestampLabel":"1:21:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- feeding program, which provides individual breakfast and lunch meals, which goes from May 28th through July 25th. And so there's different pickup points.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4873-180","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4873,"timestampLabel":"1:21:13","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- that the community can go to to get those individual lunches. And one of those would be our food truck that they could go to a location and utilize our food truck for those individual meals. This summer, we've added something, and that's the summer meal pickup. So a family can pick up a meal for a week, five breakfasts, five lunch meals, and a gallon of milk per child.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4900-181","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4900,"timestampLabel":"1:21:40","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And so that goes from June 4th through July 23rd. And it's a drive-through service that's behind EPS. And I think that's pretty cool that we serve our community in that way. As we mentioned, summer school is wrapping up this week for EPS, EIS, and the high school. We've had 55 students at the primary level, 34 at the intermediate.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4928-182","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4928,"timestampLabel":"1:22:08","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and approximately 60 students at the high school. The junior high does a jumpstart program, so that'll be July 21st through the 31st.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4940-183","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4940,"timestampLabel":"1:22:20","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And then there's tons of extracurricular activities. I just listed all the camps that are provided for our elementary students from boys basketball to football, soccer, tennis, volleyball. The girls basketball will have a camp in the fall. And it's just really cool to go up and look into our facilities","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-496-18","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":496,"timestampLabel":"8:16","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Yeah, okay All right. Well you guys have the cash flows there in front of you Starting with the Education Fund revenue projections for the month of May were very accurate Expenses came in slightly higher one of the main factors that we as we paid our deductible on we have multiple students that are in outside residential placements so we have to pair deductible on that before seek picks up the remaining costs so that was a","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4966-184","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4966,"timestampLabel":"1:22:46","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Our football complex and see these future mustangs learning their respective sports and something I don't know. Maybe Larry knows different but I've never remembered us having a summer performance before we have.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4985-185","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4985,"timestampLabel":"1:23:05","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Sixth musical, the teen edition, will be June 26th and 27th at seven o'clock or the 28th at two o'clock in the high school auditorium. And of course, you'll see all of our fall sports athletes around campus and the band practicing here at the student parking lot.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5010-186","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5010,"timestampLabel":"1:23:30","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And then finally, a really exciting week. And this happens because of our dedicated teachers, but we have a Camp Invention at EPS. It's a STEM-focused summer camp, and it'll be June 23rd through the 26th. And it goes from 8.30 a.m. to 3.30 p.m. every day that week. And so pretty cool to be around campus in the summer.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5040-187","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5040,"timestampLabel":"1:24:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- There's no RV be a representative here this evening. So we'll go to board member comments. We'll start with Mrs. Jacobs Well, um, I'm Happy about all the things that are just you know, all the progression that we're going through as a corporation it's amazing to see all these pieces come together and I'm very excited to see how the the new school","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5069-188","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5069,"timestampLabel":"1:24:29","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- takes off this fall. It'll be exciting to see all the littles come in and watch them grow. I'm sorry, this is gonna be difficult. I'm asking everybody to please keep Cindy Bentley's family very close to their hearts. I've known Cindy for a lot of years.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5099-189","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5099,"timestampLabel":"1:24:59","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And it's going to be difficult. And I haven't earned our corporation. We need to make sure we're rallying around the staff that have worked with her for so many years because they're hurting. And her grandchildren are RBB students. So we need to make sure that we're rallying around them and supporting them. Thank you. Mr. Tucker.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5128-190","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5128,"timestampLabel":"1:25:28","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Yeah, just continued prayers for that family and for the community to wrap their arms around the Bailey family and help them through this time. And also for the family in Owen County that was affected as well. So appreciate all the information tonight and good meeting. If I can get it out, thank you, Matt, for all your work you've done for us and Jerry.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5156-191","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5156,"timestampLabel":"1:25:56","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I appreciate your leadership so much. And I see Mrs. Whitaker out there. Is this our last time? We'll see you at a board member meeting. Well, I was there when we hired you, and I'm there now that you're leaving. So good luck, and I sure enjoyed watching your career. So thank you so much. Yeah, I had two of Cindy's.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5186-192","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5186,"timestampLabel":"1:26:26","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- children in class and Logan was on one of my boys little league team so I've known the family for a long time and it was that's a hard load to bear. Graduation once again was as you have often said it's the it's our favorite time of the year seeing what our students have accomplished and this was a terrific class and I'm","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5216-193","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5216,"timestampLabel":"1:26:56","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I'm so proud of the class of 25 and I'm looking forward to class 26. I'll leave it there. Yeah. I would just like to have one comment and that is to thank Mrs. Whitaker for all her years of service here. We've talked and talked a lot about things and you've","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-522-19","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":522,"timestampLabel":"8:42","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- An increase to what we had expected in claims and that was something that just ended up hitting this month The other thing made some changes to so the state made some changes to on my way pre-k funding It was cut back significantly. So the reimbursement rate is is less than 50% of what it used to be For for a program that's eligible to receive that funding that's that that's something that will definitely be a hit to us as a","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5246-194","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5246,"timestampLabel":"1:27:26","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- planted a lot of seeds in my brain that just sprung up around this place. And so, you know, I always attribute the preschool to being your vision that you brought to us. So I really appreciate you and all your years of service, and we're definitely gonna miss you. This meeting's adjourned.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-548-20","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":548,"timestampLabel":"9:08","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- as far as expected revenue for the preschool, as well as they're limiting the number of people that are actually gonna be eligible to receive it. They're capping it at 2,500 people based on the way that the budget was set up. So Heather and I have worked on that, trying to update kind of where we are on enrollment projections as far as this far into it, how many we think might be eligible for On My Way Pre-K. Remember, we have everyone apply at the beginning of the application process just because it's beneficial","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-575-21","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":575,"timestampLabel":"9:35","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- to the parents, and in this case, it's not necessarily gonna benefit us, so to speak, because the reimbursement rate doesn't even equal up to what the actual cost of enrollment is, but it's gonna be a huge benefit to any family that might be eligible for it and would be accepted. So we'll see how that goes. That does negatively impact our projections. So I took down those projections on preschool revenue by about 15K a month.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-59-2","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":59,"timestampLabel":"0:59","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- regular board meeting minutes. We have the Treasurer's Report for May of 2025. And Mr. Durnall, the claims please. Thank you, sir. The gross wages for May the 9th, 2025, $826,215.10. The gross wages on May 23rd, 2025 for $842,462.92.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-600-22","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":600,"timestampLabel":"10:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- for the rest of this year. And then we'll make adjustments in 26 and those sorts of things. But overall, with all of these things in mind, cash balance looks a little different from last time. But again, we're still showing that we're gonna eat in some cash. And really the general guidance on this is not much different than what it's been. We're in a great place with cash balance. We can strategically look at how we wanna to move","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-626-23","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":626,"timestampLabel":"10:26","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- with cash balances over the next year or so as we navigate the changes with the legislative session and what we want to do with our employee pay and benefits and all those things. So we'll just continue to be cognizant of that as we make staffing decisions and all those pieces. So move over to the debt service fund. There was revenue in the debt service fund in May. It was reimbursement of funds that accrued when we made our payments.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-653-24","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":653,"timestampLabel":"10:53","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- on a bond obligation that has since been paid off. It was the 2009 bond obligation that's now been paid off. And so when we make our payments, the trustee bank invest those funds for a period of time until they release those dollars out to the people that purchased our bonds. And during that time, it accrues interest. And so at the closure of that, then they pull that money back to us, checked with Jacob McCullin for bows on the appropriate place to receive that back into, which is our debt service fund.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-683-25","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":683,"timestampLabel":"11:23","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- So that's where you see that come back into the fund. And then other. Say what? Which amount is that? That would be the, I'm gonna pull it up here in front of me. That would be the $2,680 that you see in other revenue on the debt service fund for the month of May. But yeah, that was, and then we paid a small trustee fee, everything else.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-713-26","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":713,"timestampLabel":"11:53","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- as normal as expected. We'll make some payments on some bond obligations in the month of June. We'll make the rest of them for that first round in July as normal. You'll see that on the cash flows and everything's in good shape there. Operations fund staying pretty steady. I layered in the daycare costs in.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-735-27","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":735,"timestampLabel":"12:15","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and just trying to look at where we are as far as what we've committed to as far as hiring staff and then what we think we'll have as far as revenue goes based on the people that have said that they're interested or they're gonna need that daycare option for our staff. So we've layered that into the revenue and expenses. We have only hired up to this point based on what we think we need. We're not gonna hire everybody if we don't need everybody at this point, just again, what's meant to run it","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-763-28","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":763,"timestampLabel":"12:43","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- almost at cost option and so we want to be mindful of what the demand is versus how much staffing we have as well as just making sure that we're meeting the expectations as far as student to staff ratios. And then other than that, we're sitting in a great place in the operations fund, things have stayed steady. I just continue to remind you during the summer months, technology, maintenance, custodial crews,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-788-29","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":788,"timestampLabel":"13:08","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- There's a lot happening around campus and they're working hard just for summer upkeep, improvements, all the different things to get ready for the next school year. And so that stuff is actively going on and going well. So I appreciate their efforts. And with that, I'll take any questions on cash flows. One quick question on the first thing you said out of the gate, the multiple students in residential placement, how many kids are we talking about? We have two students.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-817-30","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":817,"timestampLabel":"13:37","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- In ballpark, what's our cost on that? One of them, the monthly cost is about 18 grand or so. The other one's north of $60,000 per month. And so right now, if you. $70,000 a month? Over $60,000 a month for one because of the needs of the child that's in the facility. And so that is one where we put the application into seek for excess cost funding through the state.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-846-31","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":846,"timestampLabel":"14:06","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And we have to pay a deductible on that each fiscal year. So this year it was a little north of 28,000 that we had to pay a deductible on in order for SEEK to pick up the remaining costs. And then that is a reimbursement. So if you guys look in the fund report, there's a specific fund as it relates to SEEK. And you'll see that functions much like any other grant where it's a reimbursable. You'll see that in a negative.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-85-3","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":85,"timestampLabel":"1:25","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- for claims prepays on May the 1st, 2025 through May 31st, 2025 for $1,149,842.02 for claims regular vouchers for 6-17-2025, $662,503.87 for grand total of $3,481,023.91. Thank you, sir.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-871-32","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":871,"timestampLabel":"14:31","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- send in the reimbursements, they send it in, and eventually it equalizes itself out at the completion of each fiscal year. And then. So what's our net cost then? Net cost, if SEEK picks it up, it's the cost of our deductible, which is 28,000. A little bit north of 28,000. If SEEK weren't to pick it. Annually. Annually. Not monthly. Annually. OK. If SEEK did not pick it up, then we would be on the hook for all of it. And so that would be something that would be a huge expense. OK. OK.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-903-33","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":903,"timestampLabel":"15:03","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- If somebody transfers in from another school corporation because they couldn't provide the services, they should have provided the services, correct? That's their responsibility if they came from another corporation. So if it's a public school that's accepting a student with different needs, yeah, I would assume that they're then responsible for meeting the needs of that child depending on whatever's been agreed upon in a case conference committee for a student with an IEP. So these are students that have an IEP","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-932-34","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":932,"timestampLabel":"15:32","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- in place. Okay. All right. Thanks. Yeah. Okay. We're not. We have the school and construction report and we have Martin True still a schoolman with his here tonight to walk us through that update. I'll try to get this pulled up on the screen while Martin makes his way up. That screen over there.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-963-35","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":963,"timestampLabel":"16:03","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I can't read it because of the glare. Okay. All right, I think what I'd like to do today","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-991-36","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"R